# Hard Rules

These are non-negotiable. Details live in glob-scoped rules and `server/api/ai/`.

- **XML-first:** schema, enums, projections, feature contracts, and generated client APIs come from `server/generation/xml/stencil-entities.xml`. Customize only the files the generator creates once and then skips (`*.manager.ts`, `*.controller.ts`).
- **Regenerating codegen:** models, schemas, `*.base.ts`, admin screens, and generated API clients are overwritten on every generator run. This is not a write-once scaffold (T4, yeoman, “generate then own the files”). Edit XML or XSL, regenerate; never treat those files as the place to keep edits. When explaining this to a person, use the generator log (Created/Updated vs Skipping existing file). Do not say `STARTFILE`, `ENSUREFILE`, or `ENDFILE` unless they are editing an XSL template — the CLI strips those markers before writing the file.
- **System timestamps:** `created_utc` / `updated_utc` are generator-owned. `deleted_utc` is the platform tombstone (declare in XML for sync/federated entities). Do not reuse those names for domain dates — use `generated_utc`, `authored_utc`, `published_utc`, and similar.
- **Additive schema:** prefer backward-compatible field adds (`isNullable`, no required backfill). Document rewrites go through `JurisdictionSchemaService` + `JurisdictionSchemaVersion`, not a required cutover in the XML alone.
- **Strict types:** named classes, enums, and projections. No JSON-packed blobs, `Record<string, unknown>`, or “this field is A or B” polymorphism unless an explicit enum plus typed nested classes. Prefer `[entity]_name` / `[entity]_id` over generic `name` / id aliases so combined projections stay unambiguous.
- **Dual-homed reads:** include `local_account_id` when selecting one perspective. Never query a grouping field alone.
- **Feature bodies:** every `@Body()` in feature controllers uses `Sanitize.for(...)` or explicit `Sanitize.ignore()`.
- **User jurisdiction:** authenticated `/v1/*` data access uses `request.account.jurisdiction_id`, not body/route jurisdiction.
- **Tombstones:** federated or sync-tracked normal deletes set `deleted_utc` (and bump `edited_utc`). Physical `delete()` is for GDPR/DSAR processors only.
- **Contracts:** add behavior to the named interface or narrow to a concrete type. No inline optional methods at call sites.
- **Privacy:** never log full Firebase UID, `auth_identifier`, JWT `sub`, or equivalent stable ids.
- **Projection reads:** a list or lookup that returns a projection uses `search="true"` (list: `find{Name}`) or `get="true"` (one document: `getById{Name}`) on the projection. Those generated methods already query with `Projection`. Do not hand-write the wrapper, and do not `getById` or `find()` the full document and then `toDirectory()` / `toBoard()` / `toStaff()` / `toReference()`. Mapping with `toX()` is only for a document already in memory after a write. `default="true"` also emits the list method and changes generated CRUD to return that projection.

Do not take architecture or security shortcuts because the first version is complicated. Cut scope only for true feasibility limits (cost, ship date, missing expertise).
